From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Humoyun Davronov
 <182140629+HumoyunDavronov2001@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:34:50 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] llama : add layer windows

Load and compute a slice of the layers. The repeating layers are numbered 0 .. n_layer - 1 and the
output layer (output norm and head) is layer n_layer, as in n_gpu_layers. A model can load only the
layers [layer_begin, layer_end) and a context can compute a window of them, taking the previous
layer's hidden state as input and giving its own hidden state as output. This lets one model run as
a pipeline across several processes or devices.

- llama_model_params.layer_begin/layer_end: tensors outside the window are skipped; they are never
  read, allocated or prefetched. The input layer is loaded by the window that starts at layer 0.
  Offloaded layers count back from the end of the window.
- llama_context_params.layer_begin/layer_end (0, 0 = the model's window): the graph runs the
  window's layers only. A window that starts after layer 0 takes hidden states in batch.embd; a
  window without the output layer outputs the hidden state of every token through
  llama_get_embeddings instead of logits. The memory holds the window's layers only. The output
  layer alone, [n_layer, n_layer + 1), turns the last hidden state into logits.
- Supported architectures: llama, qwen3 (llm_arch_supports_layer_window).
